1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,844
Imagine this situation... it happens to
thousands of middle-class families in
India every single day.

2
00:00:06,864 --> 00:00:10,681
You pay thirty-five thousand rupees every
year for health insurance.

3
00:00:10,701 --> 00:00:14,288
You renew it on time for five or six
straight years.

4
00:00:14,308 --> 00:00:16,587
You never miss a single payment.

5
00:00:16,607 --> 00:00:18,848
Then, an emergency hits.

6
00:00:18,868 --> 00:00:21,465
Your loved one is admitted to the
hospital.

7
00:00:21,485 --> 00:00:26,403
Three days later, you are standing at the
hospital billing counter at nine o'clock
at night.

8
00:00:26,423 --> 00:00:28,222
The discharge papers are ready.

9
00:00:28,242 --> 00:00:31,475
Your bill is four point five lakh rupees.

10
00:00:31,495 --> 00:00:42,093
And the desk clerk looks up at you and
hands you a printed letter saying, Sorry
sir, your cashless claim was rejected by
the TPA due to non-disclosure of a
pre-existing disease.

11
00:00:43,767 --> 00:00:45,160
Your heart drops.

12
00:00:45,180 --> 00:00:46,751
Your family panics.

13
00:00:46,771 --> 00:00:58,524
It's night time, the banks are closed, and
you are forced to break your fixed
deposits, borrow from relatives, or swipe
an emergency credit card just to get your
loved one out of the hospital.

14
00:00:58,544 --> 00:01:03,411
And you wonder, why did I pay insurance
all these years if they abandon me the
moment I need them?

15
00:01:04,912 --> 00:01:16,810
What your insurance agent never told
you... is that under official regulations
in India, there is a legal rule that makes
this exact denial illegal, once your
policy has crossed five years.

16
00:01:16,830 --> 00:01:19,159
Welcome to Be Practical with Kishore.

17
00:01:19,179 --> 00:01:24,582
In this video, we are not going to shout,
and we are not going to promote any
insurance policies.

18
00:01:24,602 --> 00:01:33,648
Today, let's look at the real IRDAI rules,
see who really says no, and learn the
step-by-step way to get your money back.

19
00:01:33,668 --> 00:01:37,416
Let's break it down... in plain, simple
English.

20
00:01:37,436 --> 00:01:41,472
First... who actually says no to you at
the hospital desk?

21
00:01:41,492 --> 00:01:47,735
Most people think it's the insurance
company sitting there evaluating your
medical reports.

22
00:01:47,755 --> 00:01:50,407
But in reality, it's a middleman called a
TPA...

23
00:01:50,427 --> 00:01:52,362
Third Party Administrator.

24
00:01:52,382 --> 00:01:55,734
Many think a TPA is a neutral government
doctor.

25
00:01:55,754 --> 00:01:56,887
It is not.

26
00:01:56,907 --> 00:02:02,784
A TPA is a company hired and paid by the
insurance company to process medical
bills.

27
00:02:02,804 --> 00:02:08,021
In India, about seven out of every ten
health claims are settled through TPAs.

28
00:02:08,041 --> 00:02:15,617
Under IRDAI rules, no claim can be
rejected without the approval of the
insurance company's own claims review
committee.

29
00:02:15,637 --> 00:02:19,621
But here are the three excuses you will
often see on these letters.

30
00:02:19,641 --> 00:02:21,067
Excuse Number One.

31
00:02:21,087 --> 00:02:23,881
Non-disclosure of pre-existing condition.

32
00:02:23,901 --> 00:02:26,945
Suppose you were admitted for a broken leg
or dengue.

33
00:02:26,965 --> 00:02:29,710
A junior doctor writes one line in your
notes.

34
00:02:29,730 --> 00:02:31,878
Patient has mild blood pressure.

35
00:02:31,898 --> 00:02:33,947
The reviewer sees that one line.

36
00:02:33,967 --> 00:02:37,478
He opens your proposal form from five
years ago, and says...

37
00:02:37,498 --> 00:02:39,113
You didn't declare blood pressure.

38
00:02:39,133 --> 00:02:40,766
Cashless denied.

39
00:02:40,786 --> 00:02:45,181
Wait... does blood pressure cause a broken
leg or a dengue infection?

40
00:02:45,201 --> 00:02:46,371
Of course not.

41
00:02:46,391 --> 00:02:50,581
But in the first five years of your
policy, the company can still use it.

42
00:02:50,601 --> 00:02:52,928
After five years, the rule changes.

43
00:02:52,948 --> 00:02:54,307
Excuse Number Two.

44
00:02:54,327 --> 00:02:56,189
Not medically necessary.

45
00:02:56,209 --> 00:03:01,158
They say your treatment could have been
done as an outpatient visit without
staying in hospital.

46
00:03:01,178 --> 00:03:02,732
And Excuse Number Three.

47
00:03:02,752 --> 00:03:05,615
Room rent limit, and proportionate
deduction.

48
00:03:05,635 --> 00:03:11,290
Say your policy allows a room of five
thousand rupees a day, but you took an
eight thousand rupee room.

49
00:03:11,310 --> 00:03:14,013
They don't just deduct the three thousand
rupee difference.

50
00:03:14,033 --> 00:03:20,683
They pay only five out of every eight
rupees... on the surgery, doctor, and
nursing charges too.

51
00:03:20,703 --> 00:03:25,443
That is a cut of about thirty-seven
percent on those charges.

52
00:03:25,463 --> 00:03:30,607
When a family sees that technical
rejection letter, they feel completely
helpless.

53
00:03:30,627 --> 00:03:33,018
They think the door is closed forever.

54
00:03:33,038 --> 00:03:34,115
It is not.

55
00:03:34,135 --> 00:03:37,448
A cashless denial... is NOT a claim
rejection.

56
00:03:37,468 --> 00:03:40,687
Your legal right to the money is still
alive.

57
00:03:40,707 --> 00:03:42,248
Now listen carefully.

58
00:03:42,268 --> 00:03:46,827
This may be the single most important rule
in Indian health insurance.

59
00:03:46,847 --> 00:03:49,384
It is called the moratorium period.

60
00:03:49,404 --> 00:03:51,866
Earlier, this period was eight years.

61
00:03:51,886 --> 00:03:57,772
But in twenty twenty-four, the IRDAI
brought it down from eight years to five
years.

62
00:03:57,792 --> 00:04:02,800
That means sixty continuous months in a
row, with no break in your policy.

63
00:04:02,820 --> 00:04:04,599
So, what does it mean for you?

64
00:04:08,743 --> 00:04:19,938
After five years of continuous cover, the
insurance company legally CANNOT question
your policy or your claim on grounds of
non-disclosure, like an old disease you
did not mention.

65
00:04:19,958 --> 00:04:21,026
Read that again.

66
00:04:21,046 --> 00:04:25,963
After five years, an old health history
cannot be used as an excuse.

67
00:04:25,983 --> 00:04:28,279
There is only one single exception.

68
00:04:28,299 --> 00:04:31,539
Proven fraud that the company has to
establish.

69
00:04:31,559 --> 00:04:37,496
Not a forgotten fever, not an undiagnosed
ache... active, deliberate fraud.

70
00:04:37,516 --> 00:04:44,647
Your normal policy limits and exclusions
still apply, and if you port your policy
to another insurer, your years move with
you.

71
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:48,465
If you cancel and buy a new one, the count
resets to zero.

72
00:04:48,485 --> 00:04:51,046
Now think about our family at the billing
counter.

73
00:04:51,066 --> 00:04:53,418
Six years of continuous policy.

74
00:04:53,438 --> 00:04:55,790
A letter that says non-disclosure.

75
00:04:55,810 --> 00:04:59,658
That excuse directly violates the IRDAI
rule.

76
00:04:59,678 --> 00:05:02,524
And there is one more rule... a clock.

77
00:05:02,544 --> 00:05:10,273
When the hospital sends the final
discharge request to the insurance
company, the company must give final
approval within three hours.

78
00:05:10,293 --> 00:05:14,294
IRDAI mandates that the patient should not
be made to wait.

79
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:24,239
If the approval comes later than three
hours, any extra amount the hospital
charges for that delay is paid by the
insurance company from its own funds...
not by you.

80
00:05:24,259 --> 00:05:28,097
Remember this rule, and ask for it at the
discharge counter.

81
00:05:28,117 --> 00:05:32,441
So, what should you do if your cashless is
denied at the counter tonight?

82
00:05:32,461 --> 00:05:34,592
Do not shout at hospital staff.

83
00:05:34,612 --> 00:05:36,145
Do not panic.

84
00:05:36,165 --> 00:05:37,937
Follow these four steps.

85
00:05:37,957 --> 00:05:38,960
Step One.

86
00:05:38,980 --> 00:05:41,118
Collect your papers before you leave.

87
00:05:41,138 --> 00:05:43,657
If you have to pay the bill yourself, pay
it.

88
00:05:43,677 --> 00:05:54,266
But before leaving the hospital, ask for
copies of the discharge summary, the final
itemized bill, all test reports, pharmacy
receipts, and the written cashless denial
letter.

89
00:05:54,286 --> 00:06:00,977
If they claimed admission was not needed,
ask your treating doctor for a short
clinical justification certificate.

90
00:06:00,997 --> 00:06:01,961
Step Two.

91
00:06:01,981 --> 00:06:05,841
File for reimbursement within fifteen to
thirty days of discharge.

92
00:06:05,861 --> 00:06:08,144
Check your policy for your exact limit.

93
00:06:08,164 --> 00:06:13,857
If they reject it, write a calm, formal
email to the company's Grievance Redressal
Officer.

94
00:06:13,877 --> 00:06:23,208
State your policy number, claim number and
amount, and if your policy has crossed
five years, quote the IRDAI five-year
moratorium rule.

95
00:06:23,228 --> 00:06:26,139
The company must reply within fourteen
days.

96
00:06:26,159 --> 00:06:27,191
Step Three.

97
00:06:27,211 --> 00:06:29,314
Register on Bima Bharosa.

98
00:06:29,334 --> 00:06:37,642
If the company ignores you or sends the
same generic rejection, go to
bimabharosa.irdai.gov.in.

99
00:06:37,662 --> 00:06:43,772
This is the regulator's own portal, and
complaints filed here are tracked directly
by the IRDAI.

100
00:06:43,792 --> 00:06:44,891
And Step Four.

101
00:06:44,911 --> 00:06:46,757
The Insurance Ombudsman.

102
00:06:46,777 --> 00:06:56,399
If the company still refuses after thirty
days, you do NOT need a consumer court
case, and you do NOT need an expensive
lawyer.

103
00:06:56,419 --> 00:06:59,259
Go to the official website, cioins.co.in.

104
00:07:02,567 --> 00:07:08,026
The Insurance Ombudsman is a government
body set up specifically to resolve
insurance disputes.

105
00:07:08,046 --> 00:07:09,304
You can file online.

106
00:07:09,324 --> 00:07:11,053
It costs zero rupees.

107
00:07:11,073 --> 00:07:12,712
You do not need a lawyer.

108
00:07:12,732 --> 00:07:20,407
In the financial year twenty twenty-four
to twenty-five, the Ombudsman offices
received over thirty-two thousand health
complaints.

109
00:07:20,427 --> 00:07:26,553
Of the cases they settled or decided, over
seventy-five percent went in favor of the
policyholder.

110
00:07:26,573 --> 00:07:30,255
And eight out of ten complaints were
closed within three months.

111
00:07:30,275 --> 00:07:37,042
The Ombudsman can award up to fifty lakh
rupees, and the award is legally binding
on the insurance company.

112
00:07:37,062 --> 00:07:40,925
Finally... how do you prevent this before
you even buy?

113
00:07:40,945 --> 00:07:41,841
Rule One.

114
00:07:41,861 --> 00:07:45,022
Disclose everything in writing on the
proposal form.

115
00:07:45,042 --> 00:07:48,693
If you smoke or take mild BP medication,
declare it.

116
00:07:48,713 --> 00:07:52,168
Once it's on paper, they can never call it
non-disclosure.

117
00:07:52,188 --> 00:07:53,124
Rule Two.

118
00:07:53,144 --> 00:07:55,868
Choose a policy with No Room Rent Capping.

119
00:07:55,888 --> 00:08:01,810
In our example, one bigger room cost
almost sixty thousand rupees through
proportionate cuts.

120
00:08:01,830 --> 00:08:02,824
Rule Three.

121
00:08:02,844 --> 00:08:05,077
Ask about a Consumables Cover.

122
00:08:05,097 --> 00:08:10,943
Reports say gloves, masks, and syringes
can be five to fifteen percent of a
hospital bill.

123
00:08:10,963 --> 00:08:13,832
Some insurers sell an add-on cover for
this.

124
00:08:13,852 --> 00:08:16,666
Check its price and its limit before you
buy.

125
00:08:16,686 --> 00:08:21,551
Remember, you pay for insurance so your
family has peace of mind.

126
00:08:21,571 --> 00:08:23,157
Know the five-year rule.

127
00:08:23,177 --> 00:08:24,428
Use the Ombudsman.

128
00:08:24,448 --> 00:08:26,824
And protect your hard-earned savings.

129
00:08:26,844 --> 00:08:27,701
Be smart.

130
00:08:27,721 --> 00:08:28,773
Be informed.

131
00:08:28,793 --> 00:08:31,094
And always... be practical.

132
00:08:31,114 --> 00:08:38,699
If this helped you, share it with a family
member who has health insurance, subscribe
to Be Practical with Kishore, and ask your
questions below.

133
00:08:38,719 --> 00:08:39,757
I'll see you next time.
